.TH rdpvncserver 1 "" "TigerVNC" "Virtual Network Computing"
.SH NAME
rdpvncserver \- TigerVNC RDP-to-VNC bridge server
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B rdpvncserver
.RI [ parameters ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B rdpvncserver
exposes an upstream RDP session as a TigerVNC RFB desktop server using
FreeRDP 3.x (3.2 or later).
It hands completed pixel updates from the FreeRDP decoding worker to the TigerVNC
.BR poll (2)
client loop, supports BGRX32 framebuffers with hardware cursors, and
can forward full-frame AVC420 H.264 updates to clients negotiating
.B encodingH264 (50)
while retaining decoded pixels for other clients and pixel-format updates.

The upstream RDP session starts on demand when the first VNC client
authenticates and disconnects when the last client leaves (or after
.BR -RdpIdleDisconnectSec ).
.SH PARAMETERS
.TP
.B \-RdpHost \fIhost\fP
Hostname or IP address of the upstream RDP server. Default is
.BR 127.0.0.1 .
.TP
.B \-RdpPort \fIport\fP
TCP port of the upstream RDP server. Default is
.BR 3389 .
.TP
.B \-RdpUser \fIuser\fP
Username for RDP authentication (NLA/TLS/RDP).
.TP
.B \-RdpPassword \fIpassword\fP
Password for RDP authentication (prefer
.B \-RdpPasswordFile
or
.B RDPVNCSERVER_PASSWORD
in production).
.TP
.B \-RdpPasswordFile \fIfile\fP
Path to a file whose first line contains the upstream RDP password.
.TP
.B \-RdpDomain \fIdomain\fP
Windows/Active Directory domain for NLA authentication.
.TP
.B \-RdpIgnoreCert
Accept untrusted or changed upstream RDP TLS certificates.
.TP
.B \-RdpH264Passthrough
Enable zero-transcode AVC420 H.264 passthrough to RFB H.264 clients.
.TP
.B \-RdpAllowRawPassthrough
Allow direct BGRX32 Raw passthrough on bit-for-bit pixel format match.
.TP
.B \-RdpJpegPassthrough
Allow forwarding supported JFIF rectangles to TightJPEG/JPEG VNC clients.
.TP
.B \-RdpResizeDebounceMs \fIms\fP
Delay (300\(en500 ms) before forwarding VNC resize requests over MS-RDPEDISP.
Requests rejected by the upstream channel or left incomplete after five seconds
receive an error reply.
.TP
.B \-RdpIdleDisconnectSec \fIsec\fP
Grace period after the last VNC client disconnects before tearing down RDP.
.TP
.B \-RdpReconnectAttempts \fIcount\fP
Bounded reconnect retries on unexpected RDP drop before closing VNC clients.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR vncviewer (1),
.BR x0vncserver (1),
.BR w0vncserver (1)
